p. So you'll literally do whole group conversations like, so how do you feel? Like, would you stand on this side? I'd stand over here and half the group over there, and let's have a conversation about that. So you can see how it's it's built so many little tools in there from individual thinking to pairs to threes to the whole group to kind of dialoguing and trading off, and all of that builds to them, then going, now what do we think is the answer to this collectively? And we build that up together as well. And in fact, that moment of choosing what solutions we think are to this problem and building it together for me is the most sacred part of a whole deliberation because that is like the turning point where they go from me to we and they go from that to I understand that, and I understand what you mean by that when you say that, and there are people in the world who are saying, Yeah, we could get AI to do that for us, they could just theme up their ideas, and I'm like, uh-uh, don't touch it, because that choice making the group is doing at that moment has them really understand what they're saying and owning it.

